# Answers to DISC_UNIQUE_BRANCH: up to seven 0xfe, 0xaa, then each UID
# octet as (x | 0xaa, x | 0x55), and the sum of those twelve, the same way.

# One device, seven octets of preamble.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe aa ee 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fa 7d af 57 af ff => uid 4c55:12345678

# No preamble at all: allowed.
aa ee 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fa 7d af 57 af ff => uid 4c55:12345678

# The highest UID a device may have.
fe fe fe aa ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff fe ff ab 5f fb f7 => uid ffff:fffffffe

# Line noise after the response: ignored.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe aa ee 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fa 7d af 57 af ff 00 13 => uid 4c55:12345678

# Two devices at once, their octets ORed: the pairs no longer agree with the checksum.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe aa ee 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fb 7d af 57 bf ff => error collision at 20

# A pair with a bit cleared that 0xaa sets: a collision.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe aa 6e 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fa 7d af 57 af ff => error collision at 8

# No separator.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe 00 => error collision at 7

# Cut short.
fe fe fe fe fe fe fe aa ee 5d ff 55 ba 57 be 75 fe 57 fa 7d => error truncated need 24 at 20
